WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.899 --> 00:00:07.539
This video explains what the status badges mean, and what visitors see once your framework is published.

2
00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:19.571
Every framework has one of three statuses. Draft means it's yours alone. In review means you've sent it to us and we're working on it. Published means it's live on our website.

3
00:00:20.073 --> 00:00:32.083
Editing a published framework takes it offline until we review it again, because we want everything people see to match your official source. If you edit one that's in review, you'll need to submit it again.

4
00:00:32.585 --> 00:00:43.525
This is what a visitor sees on the public page. The framework appears with the lessons and games that connect to each part of it, and a plain note that these are Fixer Nation's own matches.

5
00:00:44.026 --> 00:00:55.796
Your published framework appears like this, on a page for your district. Each of your competencies is listed with the Fixer Nation lessons or games we've connected to it, and our own explanation of why.

6
00:00:56.298 --> 00:01:08.808
Back in your portal, to take a framework off the website for good, select Delete framework. It asks you to confirm. There's no undo, so use Take back to draft if you only want to pause it.

7
00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:18.120
We don't send an email when a framework is approved, so check back on this page to see the status change. If it's been a while, email us.
